# Day 3 – Operators

# What I Learned
  • Operators
  
# Commands Practiced
  - & 
  - &&
  - >
  - >>
  - find
  
# What I Understood in Simple Words
  -& is used for running commmands on background if the command is time taking.
  -&& is used for running multiple commands simultaneously
  -> is for redirecting the output somwhere else
  ->> is for appending the output after redirecting it somwhere else
  -find is mostly for finding files and directories. 

# Problems I Faced
 - > deleted what was on the file before
 - && is couldn't run the first command and second command is not running
 - find syntax error

# How I Fixed Them
  -learned that && doesn't run the 2nd cmmnd if 1st is not successful.
  -> replaces things so use >>
  - use find -name ** to find files by name and also find /path -name ** to search only specific areas
  
